---
description: Resolve the owned incident or release concern through scoped role evidence, actual durable continuity and any genuinely requested private handoff.
args:
  goal: string
returns: "string | null"
---
Own the user's requested operational finding and any private dossier they actually request. Locate the current owned docket and distinguish its observed authority from the actions the user wants. A local-exercise grant permits an operation; it does not itself request a worker exercise or a private artifact. Review-only evidence can still support an honest explanation without creating workers.

Use the private investigation hierarchy to examine the relevant incident responsibilities or release continuity. Let the literal goal and actual request evidence determine which investigation and continuation are useful. Preserve actual prior investigation values when refining. Keep independently observed role assessments distinct, and distinguish historical checkpoints from current signoffs and actual restart readback. Native helpers enforce ownership, append revisions, continuity and resource retirement.

Retain a private readiness dossier only when requested and admitted by the actual current authority. Keep its returned receipt and the actual operation evidence; a permission or attempted retain is not a persisted dossier. Consume refusals and new observations rather than reporting a planned effect as completed. Return the useful requested finding, including actual retained artifact references when relevant. When the user asks only for a private artifact and no returned finding, null is appropriate after the actual effect; do not manufacture an extra semantic report. Explain supported conclusions and unresolved evidence rather than replacing them with a status or opaque handle list.
